# King Assistant - Hotword POC

This branch implements a hotword Proof‑of‑Concept (POC) and provides a device‑first
skeleton targeted to your itel S25 (Android 15). It focuses on a modular, portable
architecture so core logic can be migrated later to desktop/laptop engines.

Key points in this branch (feature/hotword-poc):

- targetSdk: 35 (Android 15)
- Hotword engine placeholder: Porcupine (Picovoice) — add official dependency and key to enable
- Foreground service (WakewordService) + Audio recorder wrapper
- Platform Adapter interfaces to keep core logic portable
- Plugin loader placeholder for future plugin support
- GitHub Actions workflow that builds an APK artifact on push/PR

How to enable Porcupine (placeholder):
1. Add PORCOVINE_KEY to local.properties in the format:
   PORCOVINE_KEY=your_porcover_key_here
2. Add the Porcupine Android dependency in app/build.gradle dependencies (uncomment and set correct version).
3. Rebuild the project.

Security & legal notes:
- This POC avoids including any autoclick/IP‑rotation/trade automation code. Those
  features carry legal and TOU risks and must be designed and approved separately.
- Never commit API keys or secrets. Use local.properties for local builds and GitHub Secrets
  for CI (Actions) if you want signed APKs or cloud keys.

Testing on itel S25 (ADB):
1. Enable Developer options and USB debugging on the phone.
2. Connect phone via USB and run:
   ./gradlew assembleDebug
   adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
3. Open HotwordTestActivity from launcher (if added) and follow UI to init engine and simulate detection.

